message: "If you use this paper, please cite it as below."
type: article
title: "CUDA Rust on ThoxOS: An Integration Review of NVIDIA's Two Rust GPU Kernel Tracks, with the First THOX Device Qualification on an RTX 4060 Ti, a Same-Day Comparison Against the Production CUDA C++ Kernel, and the ThoxOS GPU Layer"
authors:
  - family-names: Xaypanya
    given-names: Tommy
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4425-9565"
    affiliation: "THOX.ai LLC"
institution:
  name: "THOX.ai Research, THOX.ai LLC"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23969298"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23969298"
abstract: >-
  NVIDIA's CUDA Rust offers two ways to write GPU kernels in Rust:
  cuda-oxide for SIMT and cutile-rs for Tile. We review both, map them
  onto ThoxOS hosts, and test the Tile track twice: on a host with no
  GPU, and on a THOX RTX 4060 Ti workstation (sm_89). Without a GPU,
  cutile 0.4.0 builds on 3 of 3 stable Rust toolchains given CUDA 13
  headers including cuRAND, rejects 4 of 4 aliasing misuse cases at
  compile time, and exits with a typed driver error instead of
  panicking when no driver is present. On the workstation, our FP32
  Tile RMSNorm kernel matches the CPU reference on all 6 model shapes
  we test. Against the production CUDA C++ kernel on the same host and
  day, the result splits by shape: on the full launch path the C++
  side is 2.96x faster at 1 x 2048 and the Tile side 1.52x faster at
  128 x 4096. Both figures are dominated by allocation, launch and
  copy-back, so we make no kernel-versus-kernel speed claim. A CUDA
  13.0 toolkit builds the crate and passes host tests but cannot
  launch a Tile kernel, because the Tile IR assembler ships only with
  CUDA 13.2 and later. We describe the ThoxOS GPU layer that turns
  these results into a fallback order and test it on 8 virtual hosts.
  The Tile track is adopted for new NVIDIA kernel authoring behind
  that fallback; the production default stays on CUDA C++, Jetson is
  not yet run, and the SIMT track is reviewed from source only.
keywords:
  - CUDA Rust
  - cutile-rs
  - cuda-oxide
  - GPU kernels
  - Rust
  - RMSNorm
  - ThoxOS
  - sm_89
